  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Environmental Governance and the Right to a Healthy Environment in the Katari Basin, Bolivia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IIADI seeks to improve the quality of life and the sustainability of the livelihoods of urban and rural communities affected by water contamination in and around the Katari River basin in the La Paz department near the city of El Alto. 
The project is based on the informed construction of environmental solutions based on the participation and dialogue of multiple actors from communities, civil society, academia, the State and other actors that have an influence on the environmental situation of the basin.
The project will support research activities with young people from academic institutions and mitigation solutions with local communities that both contribute to reflections to deal with pollution in the basin. Solutions may include water treatment technology, solid waste management and sanitary landfills, monitoring and control, and monitoring of polluting activities.
The project will engage with decision-makers at the departmental and national level and seek to influence policies and achieve a collective response to the problem of contamination across the basin. The team and participants will position the contamination problems across the basin in urban public opinion to generate awareness and solidarity with respect to the affected communities.</narrative>
  </description>
